From 1d47ed37c67bc2fcd1f3c19d8eb2d6c6d0ddef7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gus Bourg <gus@bourg.net>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 09:14:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 120/210] media: amlogic: amvdec: add MPEG-2 decoding

Decode MPEG-2 slice requests with the multi-instance firmware. Synthesize
sequence and picture headers from controls, resolve prediction buffers
by timestamp and feed the OUTPUT buffer directly to the VLD.

Track paired fields and complete each request with its destination
buffer. Advertise the 1920x1088 coded limit on each compatible SoC.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5 Claude:claude-fable-5.1 Codex:gpt-5.6 Codex:gpt-6.0
[chewitt: log pictures the microcode fails at debug level; send the
 quantiser matrices in a quant matrix extension with every picture, as
 the second field of a pair can carry its own; and predict from a
 mid-grey picture when the forward reference precedes the stream, as
 the leading B pictures of an open GOP do, matching the reference
 decoder]
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
